\cluster creates a cluster following the Lilypond syntax.
Since it concerns rhythmic/melodic lines, it must be
placed inside the notes definition of an instrument,
inside a bar definition.
Its syntax is the following:

\cluster {<c' c''>4}

The line above will create a cluster from middle C
to C one octave above.
More than one clusters can be defined in one \cluster
call.

Inside a bar definition, it looks like this:

\bar cluster-1 {
    \time 4/4
    \inst \cluster {<c' c''>4 <d' g'>} fis'2
}
